  era: "1897\u20131945"
  title: Subhas Chandra Bose
  text: Subhas Chandra Bose. Twice elected president of the Congress, Subhas Chandra Bose broke with Gandhi over methods and escaped from British house arrest in 1941. In South-East Asia he led the Indian National Army, which fought alongside Japan in north-east India in 1944. The trials of INA officers at Delhi's Red Fort in 1945 and 1946 caused a wave of protest across India, and convinced many British officials that their rule could not last.
